  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Wednesday...\n\nA dry cold front moving through the region overnight will bring\nbreezy winds to southeastern Montana today. Lingering\nprecipitation along the Dakotas border will come to an end once\nthe front moves through. Expect widespread gusts in the 20s and\n30s mph. Higher gusts will persist along the Dakotas border this\nafternoon, in the 30s and 40s mph. There is currently a 50 to 70%\nchance for a gust over 50 mph for this area as well.\n\nFriday into Saturday, a ridge of high pressure is expected to \nbuild over the region, bringing warm and dry conditions. During \nthis time, windy conditions will exist at times, especially over \nthe mountains and foothills and near/north of the Bighorn Basin \nand Bighorn Canyon. On Sunday, another dry cold front will end the\nwindy conditions across much of the area and bring slightly \ncooler temperatures as compared to Saturday. \n\nA low amplitude ridge looks to build in Monday, allowing dry \nconditions to continue. Ensemble forecasts suggest a break down of\nthe ridge and large scale troughing developing over the western \nUnited States by the middle of the week. This could bring a return\nto cooler conditions with an increased chance of precipitation by\nTuesday or Wednesday. LA/PM",
